{"parentUuid":"ecf2f478-e1c0-4874-8b78-a63fd5178eed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQC2WQ5DPfb6KdxeSJVS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No .ink file needed, so the note editor CSS stays put in App.css under SQU-132. I'm checking the focus-mode close button styles too—no border color concern since .item-close has border 0, no explicit height, just padding and small font size.\n\nNow I'm working through the CSS specificity battle at the narrow breakpoint: the Electron titlebar rule beats the media query regardless of viewport, so in Electron the top position is always fixed to the titlebar offset while right shifts between 28px and 14px at narrow widths; on web it's top 22px or 14px narrow. I'm translating this into Tailwind utility classes for the focus-mode close button, working out that the hover text color doesn't need to be explicitly set since the base color rule already wins on specificity against the old hover rule, and I need to conditionally pick the top position class based on whether we're in Electron.\n\nI'm weighing whether to use the `in-[.electron-shell]:` variant versus checking `isElectronRuntime()` in JS, since variant ordering between that and `max-[680px]:` could cause the wrong rule to win -- media query variants seem to sort after that one in Tailwind's registration order, so I should just handle this in JS instead and find where `isElectronRuntime` is imported from.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":541,"cache_read_input_tokens":133405,"output_tokens":944,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":788},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":541,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"out