{"parentUuid":"19761af0-d7e5-4145-a385-27a71611fbb9","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14188664 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"68bd42ec-a6d3-4cc2-86d2-3d495637f9db","timestamp":"2026-10-26T04:09:15.161Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14188664 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-131-stack-67-item-view-overlay","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","hash":"2229cb231b001b80811f8cd22f07f96310a93a9b3818d2775a492325d79f3272","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm checking CSS specificity so that when flying, the fullscreen overlay styles properly override the narrow mobile media query rules, and sketching the conditional class logic in JS to apply those overrides correctly.\n\nNow I'm working through the inspector positioning classes across three states (editing, non-editing, flying), making sure the transition properties and responsive overrides don't conflict with each other given Tailwind's class ordering.\n\nI'm tracing whether GSAP's inline left/top/width/height styles conflict with React's style prop in focus mode — since React clears previously-set inline styles when the style object becomes undefined, this could strip out positioning GSAP had set during the flight animation.\n\nI'm also checking that border radius and background-color custom properties like bg-frame still resolve correctly once inline styles take over, and sketching out the base class structure for the stage container.\n\nStill defining stage positioning...\n\nI'm making the grid toggle exclusive with editing state, and marking the stage section with a data-flying attribute so child components like ZoomableImage can respond via group-data variants. I'm also double-checking whether Tailwind's arbitrary calc values correctly space out the minus operators given the dashed variable names.\n\nWhen editing, body overflow should be hidden with no padding or gap instead. For the tabs structure, I'm deciding to render Tabs.Root as an aside element, with the header containing Tabs.List and close button, then panels in the body, and when editing render a plain div instead of a Tabs.Panel since panels only mount when active.\n\nI'm checking that passing className to Root works fine since Base UI's Tabs.Root accepts a string className and handles data-orientation automatically. For the value change handler, I want to avoid a type cast by mapping the incoming value to a strict \"info\" | \"similar\" check instead of using `as InspectorTab`.\n\nFor accessibility, the old tabs were plain tab-role buttons without tabpanels, and Base UI's Tabs.Tab already renders the correct role, aria-controls, and arrow-key activation behavior—matching the same intentional a11y difference noted in SQU-130. I'm now working out the Tailwind class ordering so that the active-state text color properly overrides the hover color, since the old implementation had selected state win over hover.\n\nFor Escape key handling, I'm adding a check in the window capture listener so events targeting elements inside a menu role don't get stopped at the capture phase, letting the popup's own Escape handler work correctly—this matters since the capture listener would otherwise block it. I'm also confirming the editing-absorb effect hides the action bar during editing so no menu conflict arises, and that the Base UI Menu popup portals into the footer span inside the dialog ref so the dialog-contains checks still work; now I'm considering how old Escape behavior closed the Space menu even when focus wasn't inside it.\n\nI'm reasoning that with Base UI, pointer-triggered menu opens move focus into the first item, so Escape naturally targets the menu, and outside clicks already close it. For the loading fallback I'm planning to export a shared `NOTE_BOX` class constant from InfoPanel rather than duplicating the note styling string. Now I'm defining the close button's styling for normal and focus states...\n\nI'm renaming ExpandedItemOverlay to ItemView and updating the App's lazy import, along with the related type definitions. I'm also relocating contentActions into InfoPanel and moving hostnameForUrl and clickOrigin elsewhere, keeping FRAME_RADIUS where it is. Now writing the file...\n\nAssembling the file in parts, then editing to strip out the unwanted sections.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now composing the new ItemView orchestrator, keeping the flight/focus logic verbatim."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019bummS2fGb51s9JYM1P8NB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-a1f541e8 && f=src/features/item-view/ItemView.tsx && sed -n 98,112p $f > /tmp/iv_flight.txt && sed -n 702,1180p $f > /tmp/iv_body.txt && wc -l /tmp/iv_*.txt && head -3 /tmp/iv_body.txt && tail -3 /tmp/iv_body.txt","description":"Extract kept sections of ItemView"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
