{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","hash":"f9ebc6ef8627f089106194559f162f8ff8bfd35677ce8330866ef1d64d3490fb","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm comparing the close button height discrepancy, 16px vs 16.5px, tracing it down to font-size, line-height, and padding differences between the kbd element and my button styling to figure out whether Tailwind's arbitrary text-size utility also sets line-height.\n\nActually leading-normal in Tailwind v4 resolves to 1.5, not the CSS \"normal\" value, so I need to switch to leading-[normal] everywhere I used leading-normal, including the PdfViewer title, zoom, page, and status elements, matching the pattern already used correctly in LicenseFilter.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Behavior now matches, and the Space menu's Escape correctly closes only the menu instead of the whole view. I noticed `leading-normal` resolves to 1.5 rather than `normal` in Tailwind, so I'll fix that and then run a pixel diff.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016DREScxFbK7t88Xuw6pe5n","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-a1f541e8 && grep -rln \"leading-normal\" src/features/item-view src/components/ItemMedia.tsx; sed -i 's/leading-normal/leading-[normal]/g' src/features/item-view/ItemView.tsx src/features/item-view/PdfViewer.tsx && grep -rc \"leading-\\[normal\\]\" src/features/item-view/ItemView.tsx src/features/item-view/PdfViewer.tsx; cp /c/Users/chris/AppData/Local/Temp/squ129/pxdiff.mjs .pxdiff.tmp.mjs; for f in /c/Users/chris/AppData/Local/Temp/squ131/before/*.png; do n=$(basename $f); bun .pxdiff.tmp.mjs $f /c/Users/chris/AppData/Local/Temp/squ131/after/$n; done","description":"Fix line-height and pixel diff screenshots"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
