{"parentUuid":"a3f70510-d8cd-4b4a-9b80-ea66f6b1f62b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cda62929-1bba-4a09-ba3d-cc680eb61184","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Edit, Grep, PowerShell, Read, Skill, TaskStop, ToolSearch, Write, mcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_issue, mcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_comments, mcp__claude_ai_Linear__save_comment, mcp__claude_ai_Linear__save_issue, mcp__t3-code__link_pull_request, mcp__t3-code__preview_evaluate, mcp__t3-code__preview_open, mcp__t3-code__preview_resize, mcp__t3-code__preview_snapshot</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent**\n\n   **Original `/goal`** (standing directive; don't pause to ask):\n   > \"Own the inkling UI refactor end to end: SQU-124 (tracker) and SQU-125 to SQU-132. Work until all are done; don't pause between layers. Read AGENTS.md (binding). Before starting any issue, read its description and every comment on it. The comments are newer and win wherever they differ from the description. SQU-124's \"Brief\" comment holds the rules for every layer (gate, mechanics, comments, tests, verify, stop, done); re-read it at each layer. Gate: #131 and #171 merged into main, and a clean worktree. Otherwise report and stop. Order: SQU-125 branches off main, any time. Then 126 → 132, each branched from and PR'd against the previous; 126 targets main. You have standing approval to open these PRs as drafts; mark each ready once it's verified and `bun run check` is green. Never: change visible behavior without sign-off, fork the glass Surface, put glass or Base UI in grid cards, regress #174's data path or App()'s ordering guarantees, or wait on sleeps. Report briefly at each PR. Finish with a summary comment on SQU-124.\"\n\n   #131 and #171 were closed without merging, so we proceed as if the gate is lifted.\n\n   **SQU-124 Brief**\n   - Parity port only.\n   - Keep #174's data path:\n     - background thumbnails and posters;\n     - streamed assets;\n     - the windowed Archive;\n     - patch only the cards that changed;\n     - the cached library size.\n   - Glass sparingly, never on grid cards. No Zustand or TanStack Query.\n   - **Comments:**\n     - Default to none; one line where possible, four at most.\n     - Keep only race/ordering, security/sanitizing, Chromium/Electron/WebGPU/OS quirks, or a cross-file invariant.\n     - Lint directives, knip tags and license headers stay.\n   - **Tests:**\n     - Moved tests stay unchanged except their imports.\n     - New tests must meet SQU-132's keep bar.\n     - No sleeps, per-test timeouts, retries, Date.now/performance.now deltas, or polling.\n   - **Verify:**\n     - Each PR lists the \"Hit every surface\" entries that applied.\n     - Full app through verify-inkling (liquid glass), and preview (CSS fallback).\n     - Before/after screenshots, base vs branch.\n     - Keyboard and focus return for every Dialog, Tabs and Menu.\n     - `bun run check` once per layer.\n   - Rebase upper layers if a lower one changes. Never force-push someone else's branch.\n   - Changelog only where its rules ask; SQU-132 owns the final rewrite.\n   - **Gone:**\n     - Serendipity, Top of mind and pins.\n     - The back/forward buttons. Mouse side buttons and Alt+Left/Right still step through history.\n     - The item view as an overlay. It now replaces the library frame.\n   - **Stop and ask only if:**\n     - the gate fails;\n     - an AGENTS.md rule fights the work;\n     - visible behavior changes beyond parity;\n     - Base UI can't coexist with the glass canvas;\n     - something is destructive or touches the live library;\n     - CI is red for a reason that can't be pinned down.\n   - **Done when:**\n     - every child PR is green, linked, and its issue is In Review;\n     - App.css is gone and no god files remain;\n     - storage.mjs is split;\n     - AGENTS.md has the comment and test rules;\n     - the docs match reality;\n     - a summary comment on SQU-124 lists the PRs, test and comment counts before and after, skipped items, and follow-ups.\n\n   **SQU-131 (current issue)**\n   - Description:\n     - Split ExpandedItemOverlay into `src/features/item-view/`.\n     - Use the Tabs and Menu primitives and restyle with Tailwind.\n     - Delete the App.css \"Item view\" and \"Similar tab\" sections.\n     - Fold in PdfViewer if it fits the Dialog primitive.\n   - Done when:\n     - Zoom and pan are unchanged, including pixel zoom.\n     - The scaled image has no drop shadow.\n     - Space chips toggle from live membership.\n     - The lazy note editor and PDF chunks still load lazily and stay warmed.\n     - Every card kind opens correctly and reverse states work.\n     - The mascot is unchanged.\n     - Before/after images from the full app.\n   - Comment (this wins over the description):\n     - The item view replaces the library frame. Opening grows the card into the frame.\n     - The media sits on a dotted stage.\n     - The inspector on the right holds title, note, Spaces, tags, details, and an action bar (move to Space, open original, archive).\n     - It closes only from Close or Escape.\n     - No back/forward bar.\n     - The note editor keeps full height in narrow windows (the #170 fix).\n     - Keep `canvasImageCrossOrigin` on ItemMedia images.\n\n   **SQU-132 (next)**\n   - Delete App.css (reader.css stays).\n   - No UI file over about 600 lines without a reason.\n   - Docs:\n     - the tech-stack styling section;\n     - design.md tokens;\n     - a changelog line under Changed referencing SQU-124.\n   - Update t3.json, knip and biome as needed.\n   - Prune tests, with before/after counts and bun test time.\n   - Add the comment and test rules to AGENTS.md.\n   - **Keep bar:**\n     - extraction and sanitizing, embed allowlists;\n     - OCR scoring, queue leases and recovery;\n     - migrations and persistence;\n     - asset path containment and range requests;\n     - deep link and external-format parsing;\n     - ordering and race guarantees, liquidGlassShape;\n     - regression tests.\n   - **Delete:** type-redundant, trivial, DOM-basic, static-markup, mock-mirror, smoke, duplicate and wall-clock tests.\n\n   **AGENTS.md safety constraints (verbatim essentials)**\n   - \"Never `pkill -f`, `pgrep | kill`, or `kill` a PID you found by matching a name, path, or worktree string... Kill only a PID you captured at spawn, or the owner of your port after confirming it is your worktree (`Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort <port> -State Listen` and the `Win32_Process` command line on Windows).\"\n   - \"Never start a server against [the live library], never open it read-write, never clean it up.\"\n   - \"Never hardcode a localhost port, an absolute user path, or a machine specific model cache path into source or committed config.\"\n   - \"Never commit a database file, a model artifact, a downloaded embedding, or a benchmark output besides the two tracked files. Never commit a pairing secret, token, or full capture URL with real content.\"\n   - \"Never `Start-Sleep` (or any blocking wait) after launching a server.\"\n   - No calls home or analytics.\n   - Don't commit plans or scratch; keep scratch outside the worktree.\n   - Never commit PR-only screenshots; upload them to GitHub.\n   - PR body format:\n     - Linear link at the top, then the problem and the fix.\n     - End with the model and harness.\n     - UI changes need before/after images.\n   - Linear workflow:\n     - set In Progress;\n     - post progress comments;\n     - never rewrite descriptions;\n     - link the PR;\n     - move to In Review.\n   - Commit messages end with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`. PR bodies end with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`.\n   - Never use bare `git stash`.\n   - Register every PR with `mcp__t3-code__link_pull_request`.\n   - Entire hook: never create checkpoints by hand.\n   - The user's email is only for identification; never send it anywhere.\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts**\n   - **Stack:** Electron, React 19, Vite 8 (rolldown), Tailwind v4 (no preflight), Base UI 1.9.0 (Tabs, Menu), GSAP flights, Biome, knip, tsc-rs.\n   - **Tailwind and cascade gotchas:**\n     - `leading-normal` is 1.5. Use `leading-[normal]` to mean `font` shorthand's normal line-height.\n     - Media-query variants sort after state variants, so classes that conflict are picked in JS (exclusive choice).\n     - Inside `calc()` in arbitrary values, use underscores around operators, e.g. `calc(var(--radius-frame)_-_1px)`.\n     - Global unlayered `:focus-visible` outline-offset needs `!` to override (`focus-visible:outline-offset-0!`).\n   - **Base UI:**\n     - Tabs.Root `render={<aside />}`.\n     - Tabs.Panel takes `tabIndex={-1}` and only renders when active.\n     - Tabs.List takes `activateOnFocus`.\n     - Tabs.Tab gets `data-active`.\n     - Menu: CheckboxItem, GroupLabel, and `Portal container`.\n     - Menu items are `role=menuitemcheckbox`.\n   - **Item view hooks:**\n     - The section keeps the hook class `expanded-overlay` (used by ui-smoke and bench scripts) and the `group/item` class, plus `data-flying`.\n     - Children use `group-data-flying/item:` variants.\n   - **Escape handling:** ItemView's capture-phase Escape listener skips `HTMLInputElement` targets and targets inside `[role=menu]`. The Space menu popup handles Escape/Tab itself: close and focus the trigger.\n   - **Preview seed:** `seedPersonal` is present, so the demo is personal items plus seed ids 5 (Post), 10 (PDF, no fileUrl), 12 (Note), 13 (Quote). Image `me-optimus`, video `me-clip`. No Article in preview.\n   - **Full-app seeding without network:**\n     - A synthetic `ClipboardEvent(\"paste\")` with a DataTransfer File, dispatched on `document.body`.\n     - Add menu tiles: Note and Quote. Fields `[aria-label='Quote text']`, `[aria-label='Quote attribution']`, save button `button.add-menu-save`.\n     - Regular Space: `button[aria-label='Add a Space']`, then `input[aria-label='Space name']`, then click `input[name=space-kind][value=regular]`, then Enter. This navigates into the empty Space, so click \"Everything\" afterwards.\n   - **Harness:**\n     - `ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1` leaks into the shell.\n     - The Electron window can be hidden, so call `Page.bringToFront` and set focus emulation.\n     - Toasts are dismissed via `[data-sonner-toast] [data-close-button]`.\n   - **Known local `bun run check` failures:**\n     - lint: 4 CRLF `.d.mts` format errors;\n     - bun test: the data-dir portable precedence test.\n   - The PDF.js worker fails in the unpackaged verify build, on base too (\"Setting up fake worker failed\"). This is pre-existing.\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections** (worktree `C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8`, branch `squidlee/squ-131-stack-67-item-view-overlay`, based on the SQU-130 commit f0a2c30)\n\n   - **`src/features/item-view/ItemView.tsx`** (rewritten, about 735 lines; the flight logic is verbatim from the old monolith)\n     - Exports `ItemViewActions` (renamed from ExpandedOverlayActions; same fields), `ItemViewSpace` (renamed from OverlaySpaceChip) and `ItemView`.\n     - Imports: Tabs, gsap, react hooks, `isElectronRuntime`, `cx`, `InfoPanel`/`NOTE_BOX`, `ItemActionBar`, `ItemStageMedia`, `itemViewTitle`, overlayMotion, `SimilarPanel`. RichNoteEditor is lazy-loaded.\n     - Constants: `FRAME_RADIUS`, `INSPECTOR_BODY`, `INSPECTOR_TAB` (`hover:not-data-active:text-ink-soft data-active:font-semibold data-active:text-ink`).\n     - Removed: the old Space menu state and effect, the tag state, `contentActions`, `hostnameForUrl`, `clickOrigin`.\n     - The reset effect now only does `setInspectorTab(\"info\")` on `shownItem.id`. The tag draft and Space menu reset through their own `key`s.\n     - The Escape listener adds `if (event.target instanceof Element && event.target.closest(\"[role=menu]\")) return;`.\n     - **Layer classes:** `fixed inset-0 in-[.settings-open]:z-130`, plus either the focus-mode classes (`pointer-events-auto z-70 grid place-items-center bg-[#100f0e]` and a `before:` radial gradient) or `pointer-events-none z-6`.\n     - **Section:**\n       - `expanded-overlay group/item pointer-events-auto overflow-hidden [--item-inset:8px] [--item-inspector-top:calc(3px_+_var(--spacing-titlebar))]`.\n       - Focus mode: `relative z-1 h-full w-[min(100%,1060px)] rounded-none bg-transparent`. Otherwise: `absolute top-0 left-0 size-0 rounded-l-[calc(var(--radius-frame)_-_1px)] bg-frame`.\n       - While flying: `will-change`.\n       - Attribute `data-flying={isFlying || undefined}`.\n     - **Stage div:**\n       - Base: stage surface variable plus background.\n       - Editing: `hidden`; otherwise `grid place-items-center`.\n       - Flying: `inset-0 rounded-[inherit] border-transparent p-0`. Resting: inset and radius classes plus the `max-[780px]:` variants.\n       - Transition classes unless `flight?.kind === \"open\"`.\n     - **Tabs.Root as aside:**\n       - Editing: `left-(--item-inset) w-auto px-0 pt-1.5`. Otherwise: `w-80 pt-1.5 pr-4 pl-[18px] max-[780px]:top-1/2 max-[780px]:left-0 max-[780px]:w-auto`.\n       - Flying: `pointer-events-none translate-x-6 opacity-0`. Otherwise: the transition classes.\n     - **Header:** tabs (Info, Similar), shown only when not editing, plus the Close button.\n       - Focus-mode Close: `fixed right-7 min-w-[92px] rounded-full bg-surface-raised px-3 font-body text-[11px] leading-[normal] text-[#c8c0b5] hover:bg-[#25211e] max-[680px]:right-3.5`. Top is `top-[calc(4px_+_var(--spacing-titlebar))]` in Electron, else `top-[22px] max-[680px]:top-3.5`.\n       - kbd styled with Tailwind.\n     - **Body:**\n       - Editing: a `flex min-h-0 flex-auto flex-col overflow-hidden` div with RichNoteEditor inside Suspense (fallback `<p className={NOTE_BOX}>`).\n       - Otherwise: Tabs.Panel info (InfoPanel) and Tabs.Panel similar (SimilarPanel).\n       - `ItemActionBar` when not editing.\n\n   - **`src/features/item-view/InfoPanel.tsx`** (new)\n     - Exports `hostnameForUrl`, `NOTE_BOX`, `InfoPanel({item, actions, memberSpaces, onEditNote})`.\n     - Quote blockquote: `mx-0 mt-component mb-2 font-quote text-[22px]/[1.35] italic text-ink`, plus an attribution line.\n     - Otherwise `ItemTitle` and the note description in `NOTE_BOX`.\n     - `PROCESSING` constant (with `[&_span:last-of-type]` and `[&>svg]` spin). Active state is green; failed state is `#d07055` with a `RETRY_BUTTON`.\n     - `TagList` is keyed by item id and owns the draft state and input focus.\n     - `DetailRow` covers Saved, From and Size (mono).\n     - Action buttons: Edit note, Open PDF, Read (using `clickOrigin`).\n\n   - **`src/features/item-view/ItemActionBar.tsx`** (new)\n     - `BAR_BUTTON` and `BarGlyph`.\n     - `SpaceMenu`: Base UI Menu with `modal={false}`, Trigger `aria-label=\"Move to Space\"`, portal into a `contents` span, Positioner side top, align start, `sideOffset={12.5}`, `z-2`.\n     - Popup: `w-[232px] max-h-[280px]` with an entry transition from translate-y-1/opacity-0. Uses `onFocus={focusFirstMenuItem}`; `onKeyDown` handles Escape and Tab by closing and focusing the trigger.\n     - Group label \"Keep in a Space\". CheckboxItems are `checked={space.member}`, toggle through `onToggleSpace`, keep `data-tooltip`, and show the check SVG with `group-data-checked:opacity-100`.\n     - `ItemActionBar({item, actions, spaces, onArchive})`:\n       - footer `relative mt-3 flex h-11 flex-none items-center gap-1 border-t border-border`;\n       - SpaceMenu keyed by `item.id`;\n       - Open original, Show in folder, Archive, Delete permanently (`ml-auto`, archived items only).\n\n   - **`src/features/item-view/ItemTitle.tsx`** (new): `itemViewTitle(item)` (PDF uses pdfPreviewTitle) and `ItemTitle({item, compact})` with palette swatches.\n   - **`src/features/item-view/SimilarPanel.tsx`** (new): moved tile-height and column-split logic, Tailwind tiles, `ItemTitle compact`, \"Nothing similar yet.\" empty state. Biome reformatted it.\n   - **`ZoomableImage.tsx`** and **`ItemStageMedia.tsx`**: written earlier this layer (see the prior summary). ART_BOX's comma arbitrary variants were confirmed in the built CSS.\n   - **`src/features/item-view/PdfViewer.tsx`**\n     - Tailwind restyle. Constants `ICON_BUTTON`, `GROUP`, `STATUS`; imports `cx`.\n     - Overlay `fixed inset-0 z-60 grid place-items-center bg-[rgba(36,35,32,0.55)] p-7`.\n     - Header `bg-[#fbfbfa]`, title `font-quote ... leading-[normal]`.\n     - Page input uses `[appearance:textfield]`, spin-button hiding, and `focus-visible:outline-offset-0!`.\n     - Fit button styled inline.\n     - Status spinner via `[&>svg]:animate-[spin_1.2s_linear_infinite]`.\n   - **`src/ui/Button.tsx`**: added\n     ```ts\n     // \"Try again\" on a failed job, inline in a status line on a card or the item view.\n     export const RETRY_BUTTON =\n       \"ml-auto inline-flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-1 border-0 bg-transparent p-0 [font:inherit] whitespace-nowrap text-inherit underline underline-offset-3 hover:text-[#f08a5a]\";\n     ```\n   - **`src/features/library/LibraryCard.tsx`**: imports `RETRY_BUTTON` and uses `className={RETRY_BUTTON}` (was `\"retry-button\"`).\n   - **`src/components/ItemMedia.tsx`**: the earlier Tailwind conversion of the detail video and X embed, plus the `DetailVideoMedia` fallback is now `<div className={item.accent}>`.\n   - **`src/App.tsx`**:\n     - `const PdfViewer = lazy(() => import(\"./features/item-view/PdfViewer\"))`.\n     - `const ItemView = lazy(() => import(\"./features/item-view/ItemView\").then(m => ({default: m.ItemView})))`.\n     - `import type { ItemViewActions }`; `useMemo<ItemViewActions>`.\n     - `<ItemView key=\"item-view\" ...>`.\n   - **`src/App.css`**: deleted ranges 111–140, 154–211, 236–294, 473–704, 881–944, 1342–1345 and 2103–2746. Now 1668 lines.\n     - Kept: `.text-button`, `.icon-button` (ShortcutsDialog still uses it), `.paper-*`, the note-editor styles, `@keyframes spin`, and `.liquid-glass-*`.\n   - **`.claude/skills/verify-inkling/SKILL.md`**: selectors now point to `src/features/item-view/`.\n   - Also modified earlier and still in the diff: `useItemDetails.ts` (`import(\"./PdfViewer\")` warm), `useItemSelection.ts`, `shell/useHistory.ts`, and the moved `RichNoteEditor`, `imageZoom(.test)`, `overlayMotion`.\n   - **Temp files in the worktree, to delete before commit:** `.cells.tmp.mjs`, `.crop.tmp.mjs`, `.pxdiff.tmp.mjs`.\n   - **Scratch in `%TEMP%\\squ131`:**\n     - Scripts: `preview.ts`, `flight.ts`, `peek.ts` (CDP env var for port), `reload.ts`, `fullapp.ts`, `db.ts`.\n     - Shots and reports: `before/`, `after/` (preview), `full-before/`, `full-after/`, `report.json` files, crops `c1.png` and `c2.png`.\n\n4. **Errors and fixes**\n   - **Duplicate FRAME_RADIUS** after assembling ItemView: deleted the duplicate lines.\n   - **Base dev Vite rendered a blank page.** Cause: `@base-ui_react_tabs` returned 500 because `@base-ui/utils` was truncated in the base worktree's node_modules (missing `hydration`).\n     - Fixed by `rm -rf node_modules/.bun/@base-ui+utils@0.5.0+...` and `bun install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts`.\n     - Switched both sides to `vite build` plus `vite preview` for consistent comparisons.\n   - **Preview card ids 1, 2 and 8 missing:** the personal seed replaces them. Used `me-optimus` and `me-clip`.\n   - **Focus-mode close button was 16.5px vs 16px:** `leading-normal` is 1.5. Fixed with `leading-[normal]` in ItemView and PdfViewer.\n   - **fullapp script failures:**\n     - \"Move to Space\" was missing because the Space was created Smart. Fixed by clicking the regular radio.\n     - No cards after creating the Space, because it navigates into the Space. Fixed by clicking Everything.\n     - \"Invalid 'text' parameter\": cdp.ts `key()` lacks ArrowRight. Fixed by dispatching rawKeyDown/keyUp with code 39 directly.\n\n5. **Problem Solving (verification results so far)**\n   - **Preview, base vs branch:**\n     - All kinds open, and focus returns to Close on open and to the card on close.\n     - Pixel diffs are under 0.03% except the Space menu (branch highlights the first item) and the native video buffer bar.\n     - Flight styles are identical. The Tailwind shadow stack is equivalent.\n     - The narrow note editor is the same size (top 81, height 711).\n   - **Full app, branch (fullapp report):**\n     - Zoom: 156% swaps in the original, with no shadow while zoomed.\n     - Pixel zoom at 2274%: pixelated, grid on.\n     - Pan: the translate changes.\n     - Space menu: role=menu, focus on Moodboard; Enter toggles it. Chip appears; DB `space_items` has the image.\n     - Escape closes only the menu, focus returns to \"Move to Space\", and the view stays open.\n     - Tag `squ131tag` is saved in the DB.\n     - Similar tab works through the ArrowRight keyboard.\n     - PDF viewer opens; the canvas fails to render because of the pre-existing worker error, same on base.\n     - Narrow editor at full height. Focus-mode close at [36, 1252, 16].\n     - Archive from the view sets the note `archived=1` and the card is gone.\n   - **Base differences (an intended fix to note in the PR):** in base, Escape inside the Space menu closed the whole item view, and the base fieldset menu didn't take keyboard focus. The branch matches the original code comment's intent.\n   - **Full-app pixel diffs, base vs branch:** most states differ in under 0.03%, at the mascot or timing regions (around x960 and y160–280 in the inspector; likely processing or OCR text timing). Larger diffs are only in the space-menu, space-member and space-chip states because of the behavior difference above.\n   - Crops `c1.png` (image-info inspector region 960,140 320×180) and `c2.png` (space-menu region) were just written to confirm this.\n\n6. **All user messages**\n   - The original `/goal` command (quoted above).\n   - \"[Request interrupted by user]\"\n   - `/goal clear`\n   - `/goal resume`\n   - \"Continue where you left off.\" (several times, including the latest).\n   - Harness reminders asking for brief status updates. These are not requests.\n\n7. **Pending Tasks**\n   - **Finish SQU-131:**\n     - View `c1.png` and `c2.png` to confirm the inspector diffs are timing-only (processing or OCR text).\n     - Optionally check `full-before/pdf-viewer.png` vs after, and the PDF viewer header look.\n     - Create the before/after composite image from the full-app shots (for example image-info, space-chip, note-edit-narrow, pdf-info). Upload with `gh release upload pr-evidence-mascot <file> -R Squidys-Tools/inkling --clobber`.\n     - Delete `.cells.tmp.mjs`, `.crop.tmp.mjs` and `.pxdiff.tmp.mjs` from the worktree.\n     - Run the `bun run check` parts:\n       - typecheck;\n       - extension and ingestion-shared typecheck;\n       - check:refs;\n       - bun test;\n       - knip, lint;\n       - build, build:app;\n       - ingest:smoke;\n       - extension build.\n     - Optionally run ui:smoke with `env -u ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE`. Step 1 is known to fail on base.\n     - Commit with `git commit -F file < /dev/null`, ending with the Co-Authored-By line.\n     - Push. Open a draft PR against `squidlee/squ-130-stack-57-settings-sheet-and-archive`.\n       - Body: Linear link at the top, Problem, Fix, intentional differences, Hit every surface, Verification, before/after image, the model line, and the 🤖 line.\n       - Intentional differences to list:\n         - Tabs are now one Tab stop with arrow keys.\n         - The Space menu takes focus, and Escape/Tab close only the menu and return focus to its trigger (base closed the whole view).\n         - The PDF viewer was not folded onto Dialog, because the backdrop and z-index differ.\n     - Link the PR with `mcp__t3-code__link_pull_request`. Post a Linear comment on SQU-131. Mark the PR ready once checks are green, then move SQU-131 to In Review.\n   - **PR #180 (SQU-130):** check CI, then `gh pr ready 180` and move SQU-130 to In Review.\n   - **SQU-132:**\n     - delete App.css entirely (including `.icon-button` in ShortcutsDialog, the note-editor CSS, `.text-button`, and so on);\n     - docs;\n     - AGENTS.md comment and test rules;\n     - test prune with counts;\n     - t3.json, knip, biome.\n   - **Final SQU-124 summary comment.** Follow-ups to list:\n     - the bench script is Linux-only and stale;\n     - LiquidGlass CSS needs a home;\n     - the full-app archive-select issue;\n     - verify-inkling occlusion and toasts;\n     - Bun 1.4.4 vs 1.4.2;\n     - ui:smoke step 1 fails on base;\n     - toasts cover the Settings header tools;\n     - the PDF viewer's light header and the PDF.js worker failing in the unpackaged build;\n     - ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE in the harness;\n     - the verify cdp `key()` helper lacks arrow keys.\n   - **Cleanup at the end.** Verify each command line before stopping:\n     - Edge PID 24972 (:9400);\n     - branch Vite dev PID 4332 (:51205);\n     - vite preview bun PIDs 25612 and 32484 (ports 58561 and 58562; check the port owners);\n     - verify instances: `INKLING_VERIFY_NAME=squ131 INKLING_VERIFY_PORT=9336 ... cleanup`, run from the worktree, and `squ131base`/9337, run from `%TEMP%\\squ126\\base`;\n     - `git worktree remove %TEMP%\\squ126\\base`.\n\n8. **Current Work**\n\n   I was finishing SQU-131's full-app verification by comparing base and branch screenshots. The last command cropped the diff regions:\n   ```\n   bun .crop.tmp.mjs $T/full-before/image-info.png $T/full-after/image-info.png $T/c1.png 960 140 320 180 1 && bun .crop.tmp.mjs $T/full-before/space-menu.png $T/full-after/space-menu.png $T/c2.png 960 100 320 700 1\n   ```\n   This was to confirm that the small inspector diffs (around x960 and y160–280) come from processing or OCR timing, and to view the Space menu difference. All code changes for SQU-131 are written. Typecheck, biome, knip and tests are clean. The full-app behavior report and DB proof are good.\n\n9. **Optional Next Step**\n\n   View `%TEMP%\\squ131\\c1.png` and `c2.png`, then build and upload the before/after composite. Remove the `.tmp.mjs` files, run the `bun run check` parts, commit, and open the SQU-131 draft PR against the SQU-130 branch. This follows the standing directive: \"Work until all are done; don't pause between layers,\" and SQU-131's done criteria: \"Before/after images, full app.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\chris\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-a1f541e8\\bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"367e554c-a449-4794-a828-1af5fc219ffb","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:26:40.884Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":7},"turnOrigin":"sdk","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["76433fc7-af93-4f00-8078-64be2f9e1039"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-131-stack-67-item-view-overlay","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
